      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-222137",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$, $B$, and $C$ be sets. Prove that\n$(A\u222aB) \\cdot C = (A \\cdot C)\u222a(B \\cdot C)$.\n\nSuppose $(x, y) \u2208 (A\u222aB) \\cdot C$. Then, we have the following chain of equivalent statements:\n\n$(x \u2208 (A\u2229B))\u2227(y \u2208 C)$ {{field-1}}"
